--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Plain-language notice
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Dev Doctor is a local macOS application for a developer folder you choose. It
can read that folder, list processes on the machine, and show findings. It can
delete a generated or reproducible directory, or run an allowlisted install,
only after you confirm in the app.

The disk image published on GitHub Releases is not signed with an Apple
Developer ID and is not notarized. Apple has not reviewed it. macOS will warn
you on first launch. That warning is expected for this build. It is not, by
itself, evidence that the app is safe or unsafe. The check available to you is
the source code in this repository.

Please read the source before you rely on a downloaded binary. The short files
that define what the app is allowed to do are:

  src-tauri/src/security.rs     folders and URLs that are allowed
  src-tauri/src/probe.rs        commands that may run
  src-tauri/src/snapshot.rs     what is collected; environment values are dropped
  src-tauri/src/processes.rs    which processes may be stopped
  src-tauri/src/artifacts.rs    which directories may be deleted

The window cannot pass an arbitrary shell command. Confirmed installs are
limited to "npm install --ignore-scripts" and "pnpm install --ignore-scripts"
inside a user or temporary directory. There is no account and no telemetry.
Check for Updates requests the latest GitHub release only. It does not send
the project path or file contents.

You may build the application yourself. Instructions are in CONTRIBUTING.md.
A binary you compile from a commit you have read is the copy you can verify.

The software is provided as is, without warranty. The authors are not liable
for lost work, a deleted folder, a stopped process, or a Gatekeeper warning.
Confirm cleanup and process termination yourself. Keep your own copies of
anything you cannot regenerate.

